      "Why 2... A1 is lethal to {B1}: When White plays 1. B1, White's stone has only two liberties (A1 and B2). If Black plays 2... A1, Black directly ataris White's B1 stone! If White connects at B2 (capturing C1-C2? No, White can't capture at B2 because B2 is empty, White would be playing B2). If White plays 3. B2, Black captures B1 by taking it, or does B1 have liberties? Wait, if Black plays 2... A1, White's B1 stone only has B2. But Black's C1-C2 is in atari. If Black plays A1, does Black get a ko?",
